@jeremysalwen One thing we noticed and Claude vibed a message I haven't manually verified: *OpenMowerBot's LFS budget is exhausted, and it's not just missing images: a plain git clone now fails. LFS auto-downloads the attachments during checkout, hits "This repository exceeded its LFS budget", and aborts with "Clone succeeded, but checkout failed" — leaving a repo that git status shows as 6,215 deleted files. The corpus and CLI actually work fine underneath, but it looks broken to anyone following the README.

 The CDN fallback won't save it either — Discord's signed URLs expire in ~24h and the nightly job only fetches new messages, so of 8,632 attachments exactly 3 still have a live URL.

The quota resets on your billing cycle, but every clone pulls ~600 MB automatically so it'll recur. Cheapest fixes are probably moving attachments out of LFS into normal git (they're already capped at 1 MB) or shipping them as a Release asset.*
